{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"nonlegal-close-tigermoth","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_canonical_consolidation.py:1-18` — Preserve pre-change golden independence and encoding axes. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py:1-32, 107-113, 154-160` — Preserve propagation/level fail-open mechanisms and both logger roots. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_cas_backoff_refetch_baldish.py:1-11` — Preserve sleep→fetch ordering and jitter behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_caused_by_dedup_10d0.py:1-18` — Preserve idempotent explicit attribution, replacement, and blame fallback. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_caused_by_provenance.py:1-19` — Preserve explicit/derived/legacy event shapes. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_change_input_not_an_outage_43d4.py:1-16, 164-171, 211-218, 246-253, 308-316` — Preserve typed classification, exception-order mechanism, overreach controls, and close-screen propagation. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_changed_criteria.py:1-13, 225-229` — Preserve offline selection/error contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_check_build_env_locked.py:1-15, 99-105` — Preserve parsed lock/freeze comparison, allowlist, and PEP 503 normalization. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py:195-200, 294-298` — Preserve Git-scoped file selection and fixture gate stubbing. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_check_deploy_manifest.py:1-18` — Preserve derived-set, mutation-teeth, exclusions, and local-gate wiring. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_check_templatefile_escapes.py:1-15` — Preserve cross-language interpolation hazard and declared-variable awareness. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_child_env_concurrency.py:1-17` — Preserve concurrent overlay isolation and unchanged `os.environ`. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_child_env.py:1-19` — Preserve ownership projection and non-mutation contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_child_oracle_fail_open.py:1-50, 96-101, 108-113, 239-256, 278-284` — Preserve negative-returncode boundary, empty-output hazard, real-site testing reason, and deterministic self-kill setup. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_actionlint_install.py:1-13, 25-29, 79-82` — Preserve fail-fast install, nested-import bootstrap, and signal-kill oracle guard. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_actionlint_scope.py:1-12` — Preserve all-workflow actionlint scope and distinction from parity checks. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_main_push_policy.py:1-30, 185-193` — Preserve no-main-push policy, preserved topic pushes, schedules, dispatch, and CodeQL cadence. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py:1-37, 161-167, 352-359, 459-464, 501-506, 540-545, 563-566` — Preserve provider isolation, overlay shape/layering, credentials, region, readiness, and provider-family mapping. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_canonical_consolidation.py tests/unit/test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py tests/unit/test_cas_backoff_refetch_baldish.py tests/unit/test_caused_by_dedup_10d0.py tests/unit/test_caused_by_provenance.py tests/unit/test_change_input_not_an_outage_43d4.py tests/unit/test_changed_criteria.py tests/unit/test_check_build_env_locked.py tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py tests/unit/test_check_deploy_manifest.py tests/unit/test_check_templatefile_escapes.py tests/unit/test_child_env_concurrency.py tests/unit/test_child_env.py tests/unit/test_child_oracle_fail_open.py tests/unit/test_ci_actionlint_install.py tests/unit/test_ci_actionlint_scope.py tests/unit/test_ci_main_push_policy.py tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"51fa-fd8a-6e47-428f","parent_id":"ae4d-df34-480d-4c88","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/unit — cohort 05: canonical_consolidation–ci_provider_matrix"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788571312759972922,"uuid":"3bcb9c62-cca3-4a83-b034-3ddb907450ce"}